INT. PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL P4 - NIGHT

Concrete pillars. Oil stains. A flickering sodium light. One car left: a dented Volvo with its trunk open.

AGENT IRINA SOLOVYOV, 30s, wet hair, tactical vest, crouches behind a pillar, gun drawn. Beside her, AGENT KOFI MENSAH-BELL, 40s, headset, scans the ramp. On the far side of the Volvo, a hostage: DR. LEONARD HAYES-TAKAHASHI, 50s, hands zip-tied, mouth taped. Behind him stands THE COURIER, 30s, black jacket, a gun pressed to Hayes's neck.

IRINA
(whispering)
Eyes on the target?

KOFI
Northeast pillar. He's moving.

COURIER
(calling out)
That's far enough!

Irina and Kofi freeze. Hayes squeezes his eyes shut.

COURIER (CONT'D)
Drop the weapons. Both of you.

KOFI
(raising his voice)
We can talk about this.

COURIER
We're talking now.

IRINA
(whispering to Kofi)
Left. On three.

KOFI
(barely moving his lips)
He's too close to Hayes.

IRINA
Then we make him move.

She rolls a coin across the concrete. It clinks against the Volvo's tire. The Courier whips his head toward it. Kofi fires into the pillar behind him. Concrete bursts. Irina charges.

The Courier shoves Hayes forward. The three collide beside the car in a heap of limbs. A gun skitters. Kofi dives for it. The Courier punches Irina, she slams him against the Volvo, Hayes scrambles under the bumper.

COURIER (CONT'D)
(snarling)
You don't understand!

IRINA
(pinning his arm)
Then explain it.

He heaves. She holds. Kofi seizes the loose gun, trains it on the Courier.

KOFI
Down. Now.

The Courier stills. His chest rises and falls. He lets his hand go slack. Irina kneels on his back and cuffs him.

Hayes crawls out from under the bumper, tape half-peeled. Kofi cuts his zip ties. Hayes gasps.

HAYES
(coughing)
He said they were coming for me.

KOFI
Who?

HAYES
The Directorate. He wasn't one of them. He was warning me.

Irina looks at the Courier. His face is turned against the concrete, eyes wet.

IRINA
(quietly)
Is that true?

COURIER
(muffled)
They'll be here in four minutes.

Kofi checks his watch. Irina hauls the Courier up.

KOFI
Move.

They run for the stairwell, the Courier between them, Hayes limping behind. Footsteps echo. Somewhere above, tires screech down a ramp.

IRINA
(over her shoulder)
Level two exit! Go!

They vanish through the steel door as headlights sweep across the pillars.
